1
00:00:02,252 --> 00:00:04,504
[DOCTOR] We have stabilized Oliver.

2
00:00:04,587 --> 00:00:06,297
<i>Operation was a success.</i>

3
00:00:06,381 --> 00:00:10,844
<i>But the blood loss</i>
<i>deprived his brain of oxygen.</i>

4
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:13,847
<i>So, he's currently in a coma.</i>

5
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:15,890
<i>We're closely monitoring,</i>

6
00:00:15,974 --> 00:00:19,519
<i>but we need to replenish the blood</i>
<i>and correct sugars.</i>

7
00:00:19,602 --> 00:00:22,647
<i>We won't know the full extent</i>

8
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:25,233
<i>of the neurological damage</i>
<i>to Oliver's brain</i>

9
00:00:25,316 --> 00:00:26,943
<i>until he wakes up.</i>

10
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:29,946
<i>If you hadn't believed Bea</i>

11
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:33,491
<i>and convinced me</i>
<i>to patch things up with her,</i>

12
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:36,036
<i>Mariela wouldn't have escaped,</i>

13
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:39,456
<i>and we wouldn't be here.</i>

14
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:42,876
<i>My brother wouldn't have gotten hurt.</i>

15
00:00:44,627 --> 00:00:46,379
<i>This is all my fault.</i>

16
00:00:47,797 --> 00:00:49,257
<i>I'm sorry, dear.</i>

17
00:00:49,924 --> 00:00:52,510
<i>I should've been the one</i>
<i>who got stabbed by Mariela.</i>

18
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:56,890
<i>I should've been the one who got hurt!</i>

19
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:03,271
<i>I've done so many terrible things to you.</i>

20
00:01:06,232 --> 00:01:07,609
<i>But despite everything,</i>

21
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:11,071
<i>you're still here for me.</i>

22
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:14,282
[INHALES DEEPLY]

23
00:01:14,365 --> 00:01:15,867
<i>I'm sorry, dear.</i>

24
00:01:17,827 --> 00:01:20,080
<i>The least I can do for you now…</i>

25
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:26,753
<i>is support you as you fight.</i>

26
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:31,966
<i>Not to get revenge,</i>

27
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:36,387
<i>but to fight for your future.</i>

28
00:01:37,722 --> 00:01:38,723
[SNIFFLES]

29
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:42,602
<i>Don't worry about me anymore.</i>

30
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:46,439
<i>Focus on yourself.</i>

31
00:01:48,525 --> 00:01:50,777
<i>And I want to see you get back up.</i>

32
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:53,696
[BEA] <i>How is he?</i>

33
00:01:54,697 --> 00:01:55,907
<i>Look at him.</i>

34
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:01,871
<i>I said look at him! Go on, look!</i>

35
00:02:01,955 --> 00:02:03,832
<i>What do you think?!</i>

36
00:02:03,915 --> 00:02:06,376
<i>I'm really sorry, Billy.</i>

37
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:08,086
<i>- I'm sorry--</i>
<i>- Don't touch me!</i>

38
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:10,046
<i>- Billy, please--</i>
<i>- Don't touch me! Just leave!</i>

39
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:14,801
<i>I said leave! Get out of here!</i>

40
00:02:32,652 --> 00:02:39,534
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

41
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:42,138
You ruined my life when you hurt me.

42
00:03:43,389 --> 00:03:49,520
So I wanted to hurt those
I thought stole from me.

43
00:03:50,146 --> 00:03:52,148
I screwed up,

44
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:56,653
and my anger got the best of me,
that's how I ended up here.

45
00:03:58,279 --> 00:04:00,031
- Mariela…
- [POIGNANT MUSIC PLAYING]

46
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:02,867
I'm sorry

47
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:05,954
for all the pain I put you through.

48
00:04:07,455 --> 00:04:10,959
I'm to blame for
a lot of things too, Enrico.

49
00:04:11,042 --> 00:04:14,963
Especially with Bea, our daughter.
I hurt her so much.

50
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:17,048
I hope

51
00:04:18,591 --> 00:04:21,511
you can still forgive me for what I did.

52
00:04:22,387 --> 00:04:23,346
Mariela,

53
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:27,058
I can't forgive you
for what you did to Oliver.

54
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:30,728
My only request is,

55
00:04:31,354 --> 00:04:34,857
if you want to hurt someone for revenge,

56
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:38,069
let it be me, Mariela.

57
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:40,571
Do whatever you want to me,

58
00:04:41,364 --> 00:04:46,703
but don't you ever hurt my kids again.

59
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:53,501
[POIGNANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

60
00:05:09,225 --> 00:05:10,852
[DOOR CREAKS OPEN]

61
00:05:10,935 --> 00:05:12,270
- [DOOR SLAMS SHUT]
- Hey, Dino, what…?

62
00:05:12,353 --> 00:05:13,813
What's going on?

63
00:05:13,896 --> 00:05:15,231
- Dino!
- Shh!

64
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:16,441
[WHISPERS] What's happening?

65
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:18,818
We got raided.

66
00:05:18,901 --> 00:05:20,278
Didn't I say that would happen?

67
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:23,197
You promised we'd change.

68
00:05:23,281 --> 00:05:25,199
And now you're hustling
illegal stuff again?!

69
00:05:25,283 --> 00:05:27,410
- And… Ow! [CHOKES]
- Still running your mouth?!

70
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:30,455
- Will you ever stop?!
- Go ahead, hurt me.

71
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:33,499
You're dragging our unborn baby
into this too!

72
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:34,917
[INHALES SHARPLY]

73
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:41,257
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:44,385
[SNIFFLES]

75
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:46,054
- Pres.
- [SNIFFLES]

76
00:05:46,137 --> 00:05:47,722
- Pres, I'm sorry.
- [EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

77
00:05:47,805 --> 00:05:49,432
[SOBBING]

78
00:05:49,515 --> 00:05:51,392
I didn't want this to happen.

79
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:53,811
Why did you let Oliver get hurt?

80
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:56,230
- Why did you let it happen?!
- Pres… I'm sorry, Pres.

81
00:05:57,106 --> 00:05:59,901
Oliver is strong. Our boy's a fighter.

82
00:06:01,527 --> 00:06:04,363
He'll get through this.
He'll make it through.

83
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:07,241
- [SOBBING]
- [ENRICO BREATHES HEAVILY]

84
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:11,746
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES,
THEN FADES]

85
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:16,084
[DOCTOR] We got Oliver started
on his treatment right away.

86
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:17,794
To be honest,

87
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:21,923
his body isn't responding well
to the current management.

88
00:06:22,006 --> 00:06:23,758
And we are even seeing signs

89
00:06:23,841 --> 00:06:26,511
that the pressure
in his brain is increasing.

90
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:29,013
What does that mean, Doc?

91
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:32,934
His condition might deteriorate
very quickly.

92
00:06:33,017 --> 00:06:34,936
I'll order extra meds,

93
00:06:35,019 --> 00:06:38,397
and we have to place him
on a mechanical ventilator.

94
00:06:39,273 --> 00:06:41,609
Please do everything you can, Doc.

95
00:06:42,318 --> 00:06:43,277
All right.

96
00:06:44,862 --> 00:06:48,908
[HEART MONITOR BEEPING SOFTLY]

97
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:58,334
Hey, dude.

98
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:01,003
I'm sorry.

99
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:03,047
I was out of town.

100
00:07:05,424 --> 00:07:10,054
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

101
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:12,557
I didn't hear the news right away.

102
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:16,769
Dude, otherwise, I would've been here.

103
00:07:16,853 --> 00:07:18,771
I would've dropped everything.

104
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:22,358
I heard you paid part of the bill?

105
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:24,610
Yeah.

106
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:27,029
It's the least I could do for Oliver.

107
00:07:27,113 --> 00:07:28,656
You didn't have to do that.

108
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:33,786
Billy, I just wanted to help.

109
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:36,914
That's what we do, right?

110
00:07:36,998 --> 00:07:39,750
We help each other?

111
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:44,881
- [GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [HEART MONITOR BEEPING SOFTLY]

112
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:46,299
Do you remember

113
00:07:47,258 --> 00:07:50,094
when the bar was struggling
and we almost had to close?

114
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:54,015
You covered our expenses
just so we could survive.

115
00:07:54,098 --> 00:07:59,145
You even covered
Grandpa Jude's care facility bills

116
00:08:00,271 --> 00:08:01,606
until I got back on my feet.

117
00:08:02,356 --> 00:08:03,733
I'll pay you back.

118
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:08,196
Dude, family doesn't keep score.

119
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:13,826
And besides, that was only
a partial payment.

120
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:18,164
Focus on the rest of
the remaining balance.

121
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:21,959
I know this is hard for you, dude.

122
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:27,340
It's hard for everyone
to see Oliver like this.

123
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,135
I'm really sorry.

124
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:33,554
[SNIFFLES SOFTLY]

125
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:37,225
Maybe you should get some rest.

126
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:42,063
Go on, Billy.

127
00:08:42,146 --> 00:08:44,524
Go get some rest. I've got this.

128
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:48,361
You really think I'd leave
my brother like this?

129
00:08:48,444 --> 00:08:52,114
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

130
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:54,325
Billy, I didn't mean…

131
00:08:54,408 --> 00:09:00,248
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

132
00:09:01,290 --> 00:09:02,500
Okay.

133
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:03,668
Come.

134
00:09:03,751 --> 00:09:09,549
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:09:15,471 --> 00:09:18,766
[EXHALES SHARPLY, SNIFFLES SOFTLY]

136
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:23,896
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

137
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:25,898
- Whoo! Let's celebrate!
- [RAIN] Let's open this up.

138
00:09:25,982 --> 00:09:27,358
- Time to drink!
- [RAIN] Looks so good!

139
00:09:27,441 --> 00:09:28,859
The lights are so pretty!

140
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:30,570
- Look at that! It's great!
- Perfect!

141
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:32,738
- Here you go.
- Here. Let's celebrate.

142
00:09:32,822 --> 00:09:34,615
To the new Jade & Juice!

143
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:35,700
Uh…

144
00:09:35,783 --> 00:09:37,785
- Jade & Jude's.
- Let's go with "Juice."

145
00:09:37,868 --> 00:09:39,537
- What was that?
- [LAUGHS] Sorry, sorry. Jude's.

146
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:40,913
- Jude's. Jade & Jude's.
- There you go!

147
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:42,540
- Yes! Here's…
- To the new Jade & Jude's!

148
00:09:42,623 --> 00:09:45,751
- To our boss's thriving singing career!
- Yes!

149
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:46,919
- Yes!
- Boss, do you want to sing?

150
00:09:47,003 --> 00:09:48,588
- Your sound system is ready.
- [RAIN] Mm-hmm.

151
00:09:48,671 --> 00:09:50,715
- Let's toast first.
- Okay, let's do it.

152
00:09:50,798 --> 00:09:52,758
- Come on, boss.
- Uh…

153
00:09:52,842 --> 00:09:55,928
Guys, I'll pass for now. I'm okay.

154
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:58,931
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

155
00:09:59,015 --> 00:10:00,308
Mm.

156
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:07,356
Boss, we know you're worried
about Oliver and Billy.

157
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:11,319
So let us be here for you.

158
00:10:11,402 --> 00:10:12,778
What do you say, boss?

159
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:16,782
- All right then.
- Nice!

160
00:10:16,866 --> 00:10:18,075
[BOTTLE POPS OPEN]

161
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:19,827
- Here you go, boss.
- Cheers!

162
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:21,412
- [ROBBIE] Cheers!
- To the new Jade & Jude's.

163
00:10:21,495 --> 00:10:24,206
- [ROBBIE] Jude's! Jade & Jude's.
- [RAIN] Yes! Jade & Jude's.

164
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,374
Cheers.

165
00:10:27,126 --> 00:10:28,669
- "Jude's."
- There's fun stuff here too.

166
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:30,504
- [RAIN] They've got it all.
- You'd look good there.

167
00:10:30,588 --> 00:10:31,881
- [RAIN] Yes, super.
- [ROBBIE] Right?

168
00:10:31,964 --> 00:10:33,841
- [RAIN] I told you.
- [ROBBIE] Oh, yeah!

169
00:10:35,843 --> 00:10:42,433
["SANDAL" PLAYING]

170
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:47,730
<i>♪ I'll hold your hand in the madness ♪</i>

171
00:10:47,813 --> 00:10:53,194
<i>♪ Run to me if they cast you aside ♪</i>

172
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:56,155
<i>♪ And if you've lost all drive ♪</i>

173
00:10:56,238 --> 00:11:01,035
<i>♪ I'll be your solace ♪</i>

174
00:11:01,118 --> 00:11:06,165
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

175
00:11:06,248 --> 00:11:12,338
<i>♪ Let's just dance to</i>
<i>The beat of our hearts ♪</i>

176
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:17,551
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

177
00:11:17,635 --> 00:11:23,307
<i>♪ When you're crying and don't know why ♪</i>

178
00:11:23,391 --> 00:11:28,104
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

179
00:11:28,187 --> 00:11:31,148
<i>♪ Let's leave the rest of</i>
<i>The world aside ♪</i>

180
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:34,235
<i>- ♪ With all its baggage ♪</i>
- [PHONE CHIMES]

181
00:11:34,318 --> 00:11:38,447
<i>♪ Whatever happens</i>
<i>Lean on me ♪</i>

182
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:41,617
<i>♪ Just lean on me… ♪</i>

183
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:44,453
- IS THE CAR STILL AVAILABLE?
- YES, CHECK IT TONIGHT.

184
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:46,122
OKAY, MA'AM. I'M FREE TONIGHT.

185
00:11:47,998 --> 00:11:51,752
[GUITAR STRUMMING]

186
00:11:57,216 --> 00:11:59,552
[HUMMING]

187
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:06,142
[STRUMMING CONTINUES, THEN FADES]

188
00:12:06,225 --> 00:12:13,190
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:22,867
[MUSIC FADES]

190
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:33,711
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

191
00:12:48,392 --> 00:12:49,560
[ENRICO] Take care.

192
00:12:54,940 --> 00:13:01,155
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

193
00:13:11,165 --> 00:13:13,334
Why did you bring that woman here?

194
00:13:14,084 --> 00:13:16,003
She wanted to visit Oliver.

195
00:13:16,086 --> 00:13:17,505
But Billy was here,

196
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:20,299
so I just sent her home
to avoid any trouble.

197
00:13:20,382 --> 00:13:22,468
Of course there'd be trouble.

198
00:13:22,551 --> 00:13:24,345
You shouldn't have brought her here.

199
00:13:24,428 --> 00:13:27,473
She wanted to apologize to Billy
and get her forgiveness.

200
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:30,184
You know that's impossible.

201
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:34,313
She tried to save Oliver.

202
00:13:34,396 --> 00:13:36,899
She even got stabbed herself, remember?

203
00:13:36,982 --> 00:13:38,442
Precious…

204
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:40,903
Bea's changed.

205
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:43,781
I'm sure of that.

206
00:13:43,864 --> 00:13:45,574
Well, it's too late.

207
00:13:46,617 --> 00:13:49,036
Billy won't forgive her again.

208
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:51,914
She wants to put Bea back in prison.

209
00:13:51,997 --> 00:13:54,375
I won't let that happen.

210
00:13:54,959 --> 00:13:56,418
After everything that's happened?

211
00:13:56,502 --> 00:14:00,881
After what happened to Oliver,
you still want to help her?

212
00:14:00,965 --> 00:14:02,341
Can you blame me?

213
00:14:02,424 --> 00:14:05,010
- Bea is my child.
- And so is Billy.

214
00:14:05,094 --> 00:14:06,679
And so is Oliver.

215
00:14:06,762 --> 00:14:09,014
Are they not as important to you
as she is?

216
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:11,642
All of my children are important to me.

217
00:14:11,725 --> 00:14:15,062
And I'll do everything to reconcile them.

218
00:14:15,688 --> 00:14:16,855
Enrico…

219
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:20,651
You know Billy won't agree to that.

220
00:14:20,734 --> 00:14:22,361
That will be a huge mess.

221
00:14:22,444 --> 00:14:24,989
This is the only way I can think of

222
00:14:25,739 --> 00:14:27,783
to make all of their lives better.

223
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:32,872
Do you think I'm only doing this for Bea?

224
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:35,708
I'm also doing this for Billy.

225
00:14:35,791 --> 00:14:39,044
I don't want her
to be consumed by her anger,

226
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:41,171
just like Bea was before.

227
00:14:41,255 --> 00:14:47,469
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYS]

228
00:14:53,517 --> 00:14:55,144
It's only three years old, sir.

229
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:57,271
It's got less mileage than most cars.

230
00:14:57,980 --> 00:15:00,357
Uh, ma'am, are you the first owner?

231
00:15:02,151 --> 00:15:03,319
Yes.

232
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:04,987
I bought it brand new.

233
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:07,156
Then why are you selling it?

234
00:15:07,239 --> 00:15:11,368
Was it flooded in or involved in a crash?

235
00:15:12,661 --> 00:15:15,122
I'll be honest with you, sir.

236
00:15:15,205 --> 00:15:16,582
It did crash before,

237
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:19,293
but it didn't cause any major damage.

238
00:15:21,086 --> 00:15:22,755
And my reason for selling

239
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:26,550
is just that I really need
some cash right now.

240
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:27,885
Ah, is that so?

241
00:15:27,968 --> 00:15:29,345
All right, ma'am.

242
00:15:29,428 --> 00:15:31,096
I'll think about it.

243
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:34,183
I'll call you back when I've decided.

244
00:15:34,808 --> 00:15:36,769
I'm still looking to buy a different car.

245
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:39,563
- I'll get going, ma'am.
- Okay. No problem.

246
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:41,315
- All right. Thank you.
- Thank you.

247
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:50,199
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

248
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:11,053
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

249
00:16:11,136 --> 00:16:15,557
[PHONE RINGING]

250
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:32,449
[LINE RINGING]

251
00:16:36,036 --> 00:16:37,246
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

252
00:16:37,329 --> 00:16:40,582
[LINE BEEPS]

253
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:48,090
[LINE RINGING]

254
00:16:58,475 --> 00:17:01,478
[LINE BEEPS]

255
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:12,448
Let it go for now, boss.

256
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:13,949
She's probably not in the mood.

257
00:17:15,159 --> 00:17:17,077
Just give her some space.

258
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:23,959
I know she hates the world right now.

259
00:17:25,502 --> 00:17:26,712
I understand.

260
00:17:27,504 --> 00:17:28,589
Mm.

261
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:34,303
I just miss Oliver.

262
00:17:36,138 --> 00:17:38,015
He's like a brother to me.

263
00:17:40,893 --> 00:17:42,603
I've told you before, right?

264
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:46,440
I was going to have a sibling
at one point.

265
00:17:48,484 --> 00:17:49,985
But Mom had a miscarriage

266
00:17:51,278 --> 00:17:52,821
because Dad beat her.

267
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:57,576
[MELANCHOLY MUSIC PLAYING]

268
00:17:57,659 --> 00:18:01,038
That's why Oliver is special to me.

269
00:18:01,121 --> 00:18:03,457
Not only because he's Billy's brother,

270
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:04,708
but

271
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:07,753
he's like a blessing to me.

272
00:18:07,836 --> 00:18:11,757
It's like I was blessed
with a brother when I lost mine.

273
00:18:12,549 --> 00:18:14,551
[ROBBIE] But not all siblings
are blessings.

274
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:15,761
Just like Bea.

275
00:18:15,844 --> 00:18:17,387
Whatever happened to her, anyway?

276
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:19,139
- All I know is…
- Mm.

277
00:18:19,223 --> 00:18:22,142
…I would do anything to put her in jail.

278
00:18:22,226 --> 00:18:24,770
Family problems are the worst, man.

279
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:26,063
They hurt more.

280
00:18:27,314 --> 00:18:28,649
Just like with me and Dad.

281
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:30,651
[ROBBIE] Where could he be?

282
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:34,863
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

283
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:36,281
Man, I should've listened to Billy.

284
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:37,741
I should've had him arrested.

285
00:18:37,825 --> 00:18:40,911
[JORDAN] I shouldn't feel bad
or give him another chance.

286
00:18:40,994 --> 00:18:42,996
He hasn't changed at all.

287
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,498
He's still a criminal.

288
00:18:45,541 --> 00:18:46,375
[SIGHS SHARPLY]

289
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:47,918
Well…

290
00:18:49,002 --> 00:18:50,629
Sorry.

291
00:18:50,712 --> 00:18:52,256
It's okay, it's okay.

292
00:18:54,424 --> 00:18:55,384
Let's go back inside?

293
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:57,469
You should sing again.

294
00:18:57,553 --> 00:18:58,595
[SCOFFS]

295
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:00,222
Okay, I will.

296
00:19:00,931 --> 00:19:02,099
- I want Rain to sing.
- Rain?

297
00:19:02,182 --> 00:19:03,809
[ROBBIE] Oh, yeah,
he sings in the bathroom.

298
00:19:03,892 --> 00:19:05,978
[CHUCKLING] I always hear him singing.

299
00:19:07,938 --> 00:19:14,319
[MUSIC TURNS UNSETTLING]

300
00:19:17,614 --> 00:19:21,577
<i>Oliver will be able to be transferred</i>
<i>to a regular room soon.</i>

301
00:19:22,744 --> 00:19:27,499
<i>His condition and vital signs</i>
<i>are getting more stable.</i>

302
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:31,753
<i>Even if he recovers,</i>
<i>I'm not going to accept Bea.</i>

303
00:19:33,005 --> 00:19:35,966
<i>Billy, Bea has learned her lesson.</i>

304
00:19:36,049 --> 00:19:38,135
<i>Can't you give her another chance?</i>

305
00:19:38,218 --> 00:19:39,261
<i>Are you blind?!</i>

306
00:19:39,344 --> 00:19:42,598
<i>After everything that happened,</i>
<i>you still think she's innocent?</i>

307
00:19:42,681 --> 00:19:44,349
<i>What more do you want?!</i>

308
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:48,228
<i>You're trying to force your children to</i>
<i>get along when you know it's impossible.</i>

309
00:19:50,856 --> 00:19:52,649
<i>Where did you get the money to buy that?</i>

310
00:19:53,942 --> 00:19:55,027
<i>Some unpaid debts.</i>

311
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:59,573
<i>There you go again!</i>
<i>You haven't changed at all!</i>

312
00:19:59,656 --> 00:20:00,949
<i>What's your problem?</i>

313
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:05,037
<i>You think I can get a decent job?</i>
<i>I'm a fugitive!</i>

314
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:08,081
<i>You're a fugitive, not an idiot!</i>

315
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:09,625
<i>- Keep your mouth--</i>
<i>- Do it!</i>

316
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:13,045
<i>Hurt me again,</i>
<i>and I'll leave you for good!</i>

317
00:20:13,128 --> 00:20:15,005
<i>- You can't do it.</i>
<i>- I can.</i>

318
00:20:15,088 --> 00:20:18,550
<i>I'm not like your martyr wife</i>

319
00:20:18,634 --> 00:20:21,261
<i>who spent years suffering with you.</i>

320
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:25,849
<i>Your father said Oliver</i>
<i>wants to see Bea.</i>

321
00:20:27,726 --> 00:20:30,229
<i>Billy, just try to understand</i>
<i>your brother.</i>

322
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:33,857
<i>He saw how Bea tried to protect him.</i>

323
00:20:37,653 --> 00:20:40,697
<i>Don't tell me</i>
<i>you're going soft on her too.</i>

324
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:43,575
<i>I was just thinking, Billy.</i>

325
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:47,579
<i>If Bea really did all that</i>
<i>for Oliver, maybe…</i>

326
00:20:48,914 --> 00:20:50,832
<i>maybe she really has changed.</i>

327
00:20:50,916 --> 00:20:53,961
<i>I think we need to lay off</i>
<i>some of our employees.</i>

328
00:20:54,044 --> 00:20:55,796
<i>I'm looking around this room</i>

329
00:20:56,713 --> 00:21:00,300
<i>and seeing some of the smartest people</i>
<i>in the company.</i>

330
00:21:02,135 --> 00:21:03,971
<i>And you're telling me</i>
<i>that's your suggestion?</i>

331
00:21:04,054 --> 00:21:04,888
<i>A layoff?</i>

332
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:08,183
<i>But, chief, this is one of</i>
<i>the solutions I can think of.</i>

333
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:11,061
<i>One of the solutions,</i>
<i>but not the only one, Toni!</i>

334
00:21:12,312 --> 00:21:13,563
<i>Is that Billy?</i>

335
00:21:15,190 --> 00:21:16,483
<i>So what if it is?</i>

336
00:21:17,526 --> 00:21:20,404
<i>I think I've seen her as a kid.</i>

337
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:22,823
<i>Where?</i>

338
00:21:25,575 --> 00:21:26,868
<i>I don't remember.</i>

339
00:21:27,577 --> 00:21:30,956
[SOBBING]
